SCRIPT_FORMAT_PROMPT = "\nWrite in plain English.\n\n1. Start each scene with a line in this form:\n`{{EpisodeIndex}}-scene number. LOCATION TIME Characters: Name, Name`\nUse the actual location of this scene and a clear time of day. List only characters who appear.\n\n2. Leave a blank line after the scene heading, then write the scene:\n- Begin visible setting, action, and reaction lines with `△ `.\n- Write dialogue as `CHARACTER: Line of dialogue`.\n- A short action may follow the name, as in `MAYA (pushes the key back): I won't take it.`\n- Use `CHARACTER OS:` or `CHARACTER VO:` only when genuinely needed and appropriate to the form.\n\n3. Action must be specific, performable, and serve character, relationship, information, or causality. Let dialogue and action take the space the drama needs; do not use narration to pronounce a character's psychology.\n\n4. A scene occupies one continuous time and place. Start another when time, location, or central action materially changes. Separate scenes with exactly a blank line, `---`, and another blank line: `\\n\\n---\\n\\n`.\n\n5. When a flashback is necessary, mark it `[FLASHBACK]` and `[END FLASHBACK]`, then identify the scene to which the screenplay returns.\n\n6. After the final scene, leave a blank line and write `(End of Episode {{EpisodeIndex}})`.\n"
